d. install and operate the Software on hardware or virtual infrastructure that you own, control, or are authorized to use, including Ubuntu Server installations and Proxmox containers.

3. PUBLICATION OF MODIFICATIONS

If you create, use, distribute, deploy, or make available a Modified Work, you must:
a. make the complete corresponding source code of that Modified Work Publicly Available;
b. publish it under this License, including all modifications and scripts required to build, install, configure, and operate the Modified Work;
c. retain the original copyright, attribution, and license notices;
d. clearly identify that the work has been modified, describe the material changes, and include the date of the changes;
e. keep the source available for as long as the Modified Work is used, distributed, or made available.

A private fork or private repository does not satisfy this section. You may not use this License to keep a Modified Work private.

4. NON-COMMERCIAL RESTRICTIONS

You may not, directly or indirectly:
a. sell, license for a fee, rent, lease, sublicense for payment, or otherwise monetize the Software or a Modified Work;
b. charge users for downloading, installing, accessing, operating, or using the Software or a Modified Work;
c. offer the Software or a Modified Work as a paid Hosted Service, SaaS, managed panel, administration service, or service bureau;
d. bundle, advertise, or include the Software or a Modified Work as a paid feature, benefit, or component of VPS, virtual-server, dedicated-server, game-server, hosting, or managed-hosting plans;
e. use the Software as a material component of a product or service for which customers pay, where the payment grants or is materially connected to access to the Software or its functionality;
f. sell support, installation, configuration, maintenance, priority access, plugins, themes, or add-ons when the sale is tied to or required for use of the Software;
g. remove, disable, or work around technical or contractual measures intended to enforce these restrictions.

General-purpose infrastructure may be used to host a personal or non-commercial community server, provided that no one is charged for access to the Software or for a service whose paid value is materially based on the Software. Ordinary fees paid to an unrelated infrastructure provider for compute, electricity, connectivity, or storage are not by themselves a sale of the Software.

